SEP_TEXT:
The project, Hay's Spring Amphipod Habitat Conservation Project, is to be conducted in Rock Creek Park, will protect the hay's spring amphipod, Washington D.C.'s only endangered species, and consists of: 

a.	Closure and restoration of significant social trails in the vicinity of the gullies and washes where the Hay?s Spring Amphipod spring habitats are located; 

b.	Restricting public access by fencing and vegetating social trail entrances; 

c.	Raking and de-compacting heavily trafficked trails; and 

d.	Planting trees and plants native to Rock Creek Park within the disturbed social trail footprint to provide stabilization and tree cover.

